  "term": "lateral ventricle",
  "definition": "A lateral ventricle is one of two fluid-filled spaces located deep within the cerebral hemispheres, one on each side of the brain. These cavities are part of the brain’s ventricular system and channel cerebrospinal fluid to the third ventricle through the foramen of Monroe.",
